From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:01:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Fail the runtime resume if the controller does
 not reset

sunxi_mmc_init_host() returns -EIO when the controller does not leave
its reset. The runtime resume drops that, programs the bus width and
the clock into a controller that is still in reset and enables the
interrupt, so the first request after the resume fails without a hint.

Switch the clocks off again and return the error. The interrupt is
still disabled from the suspend, so it stays so.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with a test-only change
that fails the controller reset in the runtime resume; the SD
controller's resume fails and it stays suspended with its clocks off,
while on the eMMC the MMC core, which ignores the failed resume, sends
the next command anyway, the card is removed, and the following resume
succeeds.

Fixes: 9a8e1e8cc2c0 ("mmc: sunxi: Add runtime_pm support")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index c30eacb660f7..d24fc97ea5b1 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1515,7 +1515,12 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	sunxi_mmc_init_host(host);
+	ret = sunxi_mmc_init_host(host);
+	if (ret) {
+		sunxi_mmc_disable(host);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	sunxi_mmc_set_bus_width(host, mmc->ios.bus_width);
 	sunxi_mmc_set_clk(host, &mmc->ios);
 	enable_irq(host->irq);
